From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] iface-modem: do not abort when the bearer count exceeds the maximum

ModemManager aborts with

  mm-iface-modem.c:6779:mm_iface_modem_count_bearers: assertion failed: (max >= ctx.count)

when a bearer is active and the bearer list maximum has already been reset,
which happens while ModemManager is being stopped or restarted with an
active data connection. The assertion fires before the shutdown finishes,
so the process dumps core and systemd has to restart it.

A stale maximum is not worth a core dump. Clamp the maximum to the counted
bearers and warn, so the cleanup and the multiplex checks continue with a
consistent value.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
---
 src/mm-iface-modem.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mm-iface-modem.c b/src/mm-iface-modem.c
--- a/src/mm-iface-modem.c
+++ b/src/mm-iface-modem.c
@@ -6776,7 +6776,12 @@ mm_iface_modem_count_bearers (MMIfaceModem                   *self,
         max = mm_bearer_list_get_max_active (list);
 
     mm_bearer_list_foreach (list, (MMBearerListForeachFunc)bearer_count, &ctx);
-    g_assert (max >= ctx.count);
+    if (max < ctx.count) {
+        mm_obj_warn (self,
+                     "bearer list reports %u active bearers but a maximum of %u; clamping",
+                     ctx.count, max);
+        max = ctx.count;
+    }
 
     if (out_max)
         *out_max = max;
